<title>LEBANON: Lebanon BNPI bank net profits down in 1996.</title>
<headline>Lebanon BNPI bank net profits down in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Nationale de Paris Intercontinentale (BNPI) reported a four percent fall in net profits in 1996 and a 9.6 percent rise in customer deposits, according to results published in Beirut newspapers.</p>
<p>Assets climbed 7.5 percent while credits and loans to customers rose by 13 percent.</p>
<p>It issued the following results (in billions of Lebanese pounds. Rankings according to Bankdata Financial Services):</p>
<p>			    1996	(rank)     1995	(rank)</p>
<p>Net profits	     23. 66	8	 24.657     5</p>
<p>Assets		  1,665.439     8	 1,548.707  7</p>
<p>Customer deposits   1,538.871     8	 1,403.015  6</p>
<p>Loans</p>
<p>&amp; credits		476.490	8	  421.347   8</p>
<p>-- Beirut editorial (9611)  745307 745308  602057</p>
</text>
